**Capstone: the boundary engagement.** Take a sample customer scenario — regulated, change-window constrained, with an auditor in the loop — and deliver the full forward-deployed package: a STRIDE/DREAD threat model with mitigations and owners, the hardened-defaults configuration, a security review written as a service (findings with fixes and SLAs), and the transfer document with runbooks and rollback plan. Then write the one-page retrospective: where did the model rot risk live, and what triggers a re-model? Graded on the Concepts-section contract: every finding has an owner, every default is deny-first, and the handoff would survive the auditor.

